      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a much better breakdown, thanks. it's interesting how you framed it as a tension between \"self-possessing moral agency\" and \"stewardship.\" but looking at that, it feels like the liberal position is being presented as a sophisticated philosophical evolution of Imago Dei, whereas the conservative side sounds more like a rejection of agency in favor of external control. from a purely academic standpoint, does the theological scholarship generally see the liberal approach as a more robust or coherent way to reconcile faith with modern ethical progress, or is the conservative view seen as just a rigid adherence to tradition?",
